-- title:
--   Constancy of idempotents of a two-chart special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$, and let $P$, $P'$, $P''$ be commutative $R$-algebras equipped with $R$-algebra maps $u\colon P\to P''$ and $u'\colon P'\to P''$. Assume: (h0) whenever $x\in P$ and $x'\in P'$ satisfy $u(x)=u'(x')$, there is $r\in R$ with $x$ the image of $r$ in $P$ and $x'$ the image of $r$ in $P'$; there are elements $a,\pi\in R$ with $\pi\in\mathfrak m$ such that (hnil) for every $c\in\mathfrak m$ some power $c^n$ is divisible by $a\pi$ in $R$, and (htor) for every $y\in P''$, if $(a\pi)\cdot y$ lies in $u(P)+u'(P')$ then so does $a\cdot y$. Let further $e\in P$ and $e'\in P'$ satisfy $e^2-e\in\mathfrak m P$, $e'^2-e'\in\mathfrak m P'$ and $u(e)-u'(e')\in\mathfrak m P''$, where $\mathfrak m P$ denotes the ideal of $P$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m$, and likewise for $P'$, $P''$. The conclusion is that there exists $r\in R$ with $e-r\cdot 1_P\in\mathfrak m P$ and $e'-r\cdot 1_{P'}\in\mathfrak m P'$.
--
--   In geometric terms $(e,e')$ is an idempotent of the ring of global functions on the special fibre of a two-chart model over $R$, and the statement asserts that such an idempotent is constant, i.e. comes from $R$; it is an algebraic form of the Zariski connectedness criterion, with the hypothesis (htor) playing the role of control of $a\pi$-torsion in the first cohomology of the two-term complex $P\oplus P'\to P''$. It is used in the treatment of regular prolongations of algebraic curves, in the lemmas [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_eq_algebraMap_add_mul_of_valuation_lt_one_of_krullDimLE_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_eq_algebraMap_add_mul_of_valuation_lt_one_of_krullDimLE_one) and [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_forall_residue_eq_algebraMap_of_mem_residueSpan_inf_of_krullDimLE_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_forall_residue_eq_algebraMap_of_mem_residueSpan_inf_of_krullDimLE_one).
